From ba071afe7a922bcc6aa322b3a0d9cc98bb25e61a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 12:01:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(monitor): resolve PR number from runner env, never fail
 on unrelated events
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Resolve PR number step read EVENT_PATH from the github.event_path
expression context, which resolved EMPTY on the runner — jq then got an empty
filename and the job red-X'd (exit 2) on its own first run.

Use the always-set runner env vars $GITHUB_EVENT_NAME / $GITHUB_EVENT_PATH
directly, guard that the payload file exists, and swallow jq errors so any
unrelated or malformed event is a CLEAN no-op (should_run=false, exit 0) rather
than a failed check. A monitor that red-X's itself on unrelated events is worse
than useless.

Verified locally against all five event payloads: pull_request / review /
review_comment -> PR number; issue_comment -> PR number only when
.issue.pull_request present (plain issue comment skips); check_suite -> number
or skip when empty; missing payload -> no-op.

Refs: 35ee8d78, b5c154cd, c2d398e5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml b/.github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml
index 6e6c81f1..a11f3a58 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/pr-monitor.yml
@@ -42,30 +42,40 @@ jobs:
     steps:
       - name: Resolve PR number
         id: resolve
-        env:
-          EVENT_NAME: ${{ github.event_name }}
-          EVENT_PATH: ${{ github.event_path }}
         run: |
-          set -euo pipefail
+          set -uo pipefail
+          # Use the runner-provided env vars ($GITHUB_EVENT_NAME / $GITHUB_EVENT_PATH),
+          # which are ALWAYS set — the github.event_path expression context can resolve
+          # empty, which previously handed jq an empty filename and failed the job.
+          EVENT_NAME="${GITHUB_EVENT_NAME:-}"
+          EVENT_PATH="${GITHUB_EVENT_PATH:-}"
+          PR=""
+          if [ -z "$EVENT_PATH" ] || [ ! -f "$EVENT_PATH" ]; then
+            echo "No event payload file ('$EVENT_PATH'); clean no-op."
+            echo "should_run=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
+            exit 0
+          fi
+          # jq errors are swallowed (|| true): a monitor must never red-X itself on an
+          # unrelated or malformed event — no PR context means a clean no-op, not a fail.
           case "$EVENT_NAME" in
             pull_request|pull_request_review|pull_request_review_comment)
-              PR=$(jq -r '.pull_request.number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH") ;;
+              PR=$(jq -r '.pull_request.number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true) ;;
             issue_comment)
-              # Only PR comments carry .issue.pull_request; plain issues are skipped.
-              if [ "$(jq -r '.issue.pull_request // empty' "$EVENT_PATH")" != "" ]; then
-                PR=$(jq -r '.issue.number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH")
-              else
-                PR=""
+              # Only PR comments carry .issue.pull_request; plain issue comments are skipped.
+              if [ "$(jq -r '.issue.pull_request // empty' "$EVENT_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true)" != "" ]; then
+                PR=$(jq -r '.issue.number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true)
               fi ;;
             check_suite)
-              PR=$(jq -r '.check_suite.pull_requests[0].number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH") ;;
+              # No direct PR number; may be empty for forks/detached suites — then skip.
+              PR=$(jq -r '.check_suite.pull_requests[0].number // empty' "$EVENT_PATH" 2>/dev/null || true) ;;
             *)
               PR="" ;;
           esac
           if [ -z "$PR" ]; then
-            echo "No PR associated with this event; nothing to surface."
+            echo "No PR associated with event '$EVENT_NAME'; clean no-op."
             echo "should_run=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
           else
+            echo "Resolved PR #$PR from event '$EVENT_NAME'."
             echo "should_run=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
             echo "pr=$PR" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
           fi
-- 
